<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: TENNIS-HABSUDOVA ROARS BACK TO WIN WTA TOURNAMENT.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-HABSUDOVA ROARS BACK TO WIN WTA TOURNAMENT.</headline>
<dateline>PROSTEJOV, Czech Republic 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovakia's</p>
<p>Karina Habsudova, after throwing away the first set, stormed</p>
<p>back to take a WTA women's indoor tennis tournament on Sunday,</p>
<p>beating Austrian Barbara Paulus 6-7 (4-7) 6-1 6-3.</p>
<p>Top-seed Habsudova, who also won the tournament in 1995,</p>
<p>jumped out to a 5-2 lead in the first set but failed to</p>
<p>capitalise, allowing Paulus to overcome a slow start and win</p>
<p>the tie-break.</p>
<p>Habsudova then broke second-seeded Paulus early in the</p>
<p>second set and never looked back, dropping only one service</p>
<p>game the rest of the match.</p>
<p>&quot;In the second set, I tried to forget how the first set was</p>
<p>decided,&quot; said Habsudova.</p>
</text>
